 "intro_html": "A braise from the city of Andong: chicken on the bone in a <b>glossy soy, garlic and brown sugar sauce</b>, with chunks of potato and carrot and chewy glass noodles stirred in at the end. Traditionally it has a few dried chillies for warmth. Here they are optional, so it is savoury-sweet rather than hot. A <b>wide steel sauté pan with a lid</b> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"28\" data-s=\"0\">28 cm</span>) is ideal. Brown the chicken skin-side down first, then braise covered and reduce uncovered so the sauce coats everything. Use ordinary chicken pieces; nothing needs thin slicing. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
