 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Korean dangmyeon are grey, made from sweet potato starch, and stay chewy.</li><li>Thin mung bean vermicelli works too: soak it only 10 minutes and simmer only 1–2 minutes, because it softens fast.</li><li>The noodles keep drinking sauce after you turn off the heat, so serve straight away.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Glass noodles"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"700\" data-s=\"0\">700 g</span> boneless skinless thighs cut into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 cm</span> chunks.</li><li>Brown them for 3–4 minutes, braise for only 8 minutes before adding the potato, and use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"400\" data-s=\"0\">400 ml</span> water.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Boneless thighs"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Two whole dried chillies give gentle warmth without making it spicy.</li><li>For more heat, crack them open, or add a sliced fresh green chilli with the onion.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "A little heat"
  }
 ],
