  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat the oil in the steel pan on <b>medium-high</b> until it shimmers. Lay the chicken in <b>skin-side down</b> in one layer and leave it alone for <b>6–8 minutes</b>, until the skin is golden and releases from the pan by itself.</li><li>Turn the pieces and brown the other side for 2 minutes. Tip out all but about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span> of the rendered fat. The brown film on the pan is flavour; keep it.</li></ul>",
